// @@@ If the index is within the valid range (from 0 to the size of the list), then for every position from the index to the previous size of the list, the element at each position after insertion is either null if it was null before, or it equals the element that was at that position before the insertion.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at that index was null, or it is equal to the old element at that index.
